IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 2 DIVISIONS 2 AND 3: MICROCHIPPING (ss 14-17)
-- AND STERILISATION (ss 18-21), with Cat Regulations 2012 regs 5(2)-(3),
-- 17 and 18.
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 280-312; inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt
-- lines 69-77, 186-205.
--
-- Each offence is encoded in three parts (phrasebook 5.7): the duty, a
-- BOOLEAN test of whether facts contravene it, and the maximum fine as a
-- ceiling. Sentencing is not modelled.

§ `Part 2 — Registration, identification and sterilisation of cats`

§§ `Division 2 — Microchipping`

§§§ `14. Cats to be microchipped`

-- s 14(2): "A cat is exempt from microchipping if a certificate given by a
-- veterinarian stating that the implantation of a microchip in the cat may
-- adversely affect the health and welfare of the cat applies in respect of
-- the cat." s 14(3): "A certificate referred to in subsection (2) cannot
-- apply in respect of a cat that is under 6 months of age."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(2), (3)
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt from microchipping` cat `on` d IF
    CONSIDER cat's `certificate against microchipping`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST c   THEN     "(2)" ... c's `given by a veterinarian`
                       AND c's `states the procedure may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare`
                       AND "(3)" ... `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (cat's `date of birth`) `, on` d

-- s 14(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure
-- that the cat is microchipped, unless the cat is exempt from microchipping."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(1)
GIVEN d   IS A DATE
      p   IS A Person
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1) is contravened on` d `by` p `as to` cat IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (cat's `date of birth`) `, on` d
    AND NOT `microchipped` cat
    AND NOT `exempt from microchipping` cat `on` d

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 14(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `15. Microchip implanter to give information to microchip database company`

-- s 15: "A microchip implanter who implants a microchip in a cat must,
-- within 7 days after the microchip is implanted, give notice in writing in
-- the form, if any, prescribed of the information prescribed to the
-- microchip database company for that cat." No form is prescribed; reg 17
-- prescribes the information.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 17
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 17 — information the implanter must give` MEANS
    LIST "(a) the microchip barcode information or sticker"
       , "(b) the microchip number"
       , "(c) the microchip implanter's full name"
       , "(d) if the microchip implanter is a part of a company or organisation, the name of that company or organisation"
       , "(e) full contact details for the microchip implanter's company or organisation (if applicable)"
       , "(f) the date the cat was microchipped"
       , "(g) the cat owner's full name"
       , "(h) the cat owner's residential address"
       , "(i) the cat owner's contact telephone numbers — home, work and mobile"
       , "(j) the cat owner's email address"
       , "(k) the address at which the cat is normally kept"
       , "(l) the cat's name"
       , "(m) the age, breed (if known), colour, gender and sterilisation status of the cat"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 15 — the implanter's duty, counted in days from the implantation` MEANS
    PARTY `the microchip implanter`
    MUST  `give the microchip database company notice of the prescribed information`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the microchip implanter` BECAUSE "s 15: the prescribed information was not given to the microchip database company within 7 days after the microchip was implanted"

-- The same duty on the calendar (Interpretation Act s 61(1)(b), (e)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15
GIVEN d                 IS A DATE
      dev               IS AN `Implanted device`
      `notice given on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      holidays          IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15 is contravened on` d `as to` dev `, notice given on` `notice given on` `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `a microchip implanter` (dev's `implanted by`)
    AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (dev's `date implanted`) `, done on` `notice given on` `, as at` d `given` holidays

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `16. Microchip database company's obligations`

-- s 16: "A microchip database company for a cat must keep and maintain in
-- its microchip database the information prescribed under section 15 in
-- respect of the cat." Whether it did is an input.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 16
GIVEN `keeps and maintains the reg 17 information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16 is contravened, where the company` `keeps and maintains the reg 17 information` IF
    NOT `keeps and maintains the reg 17 information`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 16 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 16 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `17. Interference with microchips`

-- s 17: "A person must not, without reasonable excuse, remove or interfere
-- with a microchip implanted in a cat."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 17
GIVEN `removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a cat` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had a reasonable excuse`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17 is contravened, where the person` `removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a cat` `and the excuse is` `had a reasonable excuse` IF
        `removed or interfered with a microchip implanted in a cat`
    AND NOT "without reasonable excuse" ... `had a reasonable excuse`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 17 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 17 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `reg 5(2), (3) — microchips that do not comply`

-- reg 5(2): "A person must not sell, supply or provide a microchip for
-- microchipping a cat, unless the microchip complies with subregulation (1)."
-- reg 5(3): "A microchip implanter must not implant a microchip in a cat,
-- unless the microchip complies with subregulation (1)."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 5(2)
GIVEN dev IS AN `Implanted device`
      `sold, supplied or provided it for microchipping a cat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 5(2) is contravened as to` dev `, where the person` `sold, supplied or provided it for microchipping a cat` IF
        `sold, supplied or provided it for microchipping a cat`
    AND NOT `of a prescribed type` dev

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 5(3)
GIVEN dev IS AN `Implanted device`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 5(3) is contravened by implanting` dev IF
        `a microchip implanter` (dev's `implanted by`)
    AND NOT `of a prescribed type` dev

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 5(2), (3) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§ `Division 3 — Sterilisation`

§§§ `18. Cats to be sterilised`

-- s 18(2)(c): "the cat belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from
-- sterilisation." No regulation under the Act prescribes one: not the Cat
-- Regulations 2012 (reg 9 prescribes exemption from REGISTRATION, under
-- ss 5(2)(c) and 9(2)(b), and says so in its heading), and not the Cat
-- (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013 (inputs/PROVENANCE.md). That
-- is the law's own answer — no class — not a gap.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(2)(c); Cat Regulations 2012 (no regulation under s 18(2)(c))
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` cat IF
    FALSE

-- s 18(2): "A cat is exempt from sterilisation if any of the following apply
-- in respect of the cat — (a) a certificate given by a veterinarian stating
-- that to sterilise the cat may adversely affect the health and welfare of
-- the cat applies in respect of the cat; (b) the cat is owned, for the
-- purpose of breeding, by an approved cat breeder; (c) the cat belongs to a
-- class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation."
-- s 18(3): a certificate "cannot apply in respect of a cat that is under 6
-- months of age."
--
-- (b) needs to know WHO owns the cat. `people` is everyone the caller knows
-- of; (b) is met if any of them is an owner on d and an approved cat breeder.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(2), (3)
GIVEN cat    IS A Cat
      d      IS A DATE
      people IS A LIST OF Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt from sterilisation` cat `on` d `, its owners among` people IF
        "(a)" ... `a certificate applies`
    ..  "(b)" ... cat's `owned for the purpose of breeding`
              AND any (GIVEN p YIELD `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p AND `an approved cat breeder` p) people
    OR  "(c)" ... `belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` cat
    WHERE
        `a certificate applies` MEANS
            CONSIDER cat's `certificate against sterilisation`
            WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST c   THEN     c's `given by a veterinarian`
                               AND c's `states the procedure may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare`
                               AND "(3)" ... `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (cat's `date of birth`) `, on` d

-- s 18(1): "The owner of a cat that has reached 6 months of age must ensure
-- that the cat is sterilised by a veterinarian, unless the cat is exempt
-- from sterilisation."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(1)
GIVEN d      IS A DATE
      p      IS A Person
      cat    IS A Cat
      people IS A LIST OF Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1) is contravened on` d `by` p `as to` cat `, its owners among` people IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p
    AND `reached` 6 `months of age, if born on` (cat's `date of birth`) `, on` d
    AND NOT `sterilised by a veterinarian`
    AND NOT `exempt from sterilisation` cat `on` d `, its owners among` people
    WHERE
        `sterilised by a veterinarian` MEANS
            CONSIDER cat's `sterilising procedure`
            WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST sp  THEN `sterilised` cat AND sp's `performed by a veterinarian`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 18(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `19. Identifying as sterilised a cat that is not sterilised`

-- s 19: "A person must not identify a cat as sterilised in the manner
-- prescribed if it is not sterilised." reg 18(1): "A cat is identified as
-- sterilised by a sterilisation certificate given in relation to that cat
-- under section 21 of the Act or a sterilisation tattoo on the cat's ear."
-- reg 18(2): the tattoo is "a broken circle with a bisecting broken line".
-- (the type is declared in cat-domain.l4)

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 18(1)
GIVEN m IS A `Means of identifying a cat as sterilised`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a manner prescribed for identifying a cat as sterilised` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a sterilisation certificate given under section 21` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sterilisation tattoo on the cat's ear`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some other means`                                   THEN FALSE

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 19; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 18
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
      m   IS A `Means of identifying a cat as sterilised`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19 is contravened by identifying` cat `as sterilised by` m IF
        `a manner prescribed for identifying a cat as sterilised` m
    AND NOT `sterilised` cat

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 19 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 19 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `20. Notice of sterilisation to be given to microchip database company`

-- s 20: "A veterinarian who sterilises a microchipped cat must, within 7
-- days after sterilising the cat, give notice in writing in the form, if
-- any, prescribed of the sterilisation of the cat to the microchip database
-- company for that cat." No form is prescribed.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 20 — the veterinarian's duty, counted in days from the sterilisation` MEANS
    PARTY `the veterinarian`
    MUST  `give the microchip database company notice of the sterilisation`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the veterinarian` BECAUSE "s 20: notice of the sterilisation was not given to the microchip database company within 7 days after sterilising the cat"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20
GIVEN d                 IS A DATE
      cat               IS A Cat
      `notice given on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      holidays          IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 is contravened on` d `as to` cat `, notice given on` `notice given on` `given` holidays IF
    `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `microchipped` cat
    AND CONSIDER cat's `sterilising procedure`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST sp THEN     sp's `performed by a veterinarian`
                          AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (sp's `date performed`) `, done on` `notice given on` `, as at` d `given` holidays

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 20 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `21. Certificate of sterilisation to be given`

-- s 21: "A veterinarian who sterilises a cat must give a certificate of
-- sterilisation to the owner of the cat." The section fixes no time, so the
-- Interpretation Act s 63 applies ("with all convenient speed"): whether a
-- certificate not yet given has been withheld too long is a judgement, and
-- an input here.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 21; Interpretation Act 1984 s 63
GIVEN `sterilised the cat`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave the owner a certificate of sterilisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for giving it has passed`        IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21 is contravened, where the veterinarian` `sterilised the cat` `, gave a certificate` `gave the owner a certificate of sterilisation` `, and time has passed` `the time for giving it has passed` IF
        `sterilised the cat`
    AND NOT `gave the owner a certificate of sterilisation`
    AND `the time for giving it has passed`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 21 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 21 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000
